recovery(r3): add linux,code to u-boot button nodes so `button reset` works

u-boot's button_gpio_probe() requires a linux,code property:
    ret = dev_read_u32(dev, "linux,code", &priv->linux_code);
    return ret;            /* -EINVAL (-22) when the property is absent */
R3 button nodes (mt7986a-bpi-r3-sd.dts, #included by -emmc.dts) set only
label + gpios, no linux,code -> probe fails, so `button reset` (used by the
A/B bootcmd to trigger golden_restore) reports not-found (err -22; the reset
key also shows -16 on a second try, the first failed probe leaves pio9
claimed) and L4 recovery can never fire. R4 / r4-lite button nodes carry
linux,code and work. Add it (reset = KEY_RESTART on physical reset pio9,
wps = KEY_WPS_BUTTON on pio10). DTS-only; mt7986 pinctrl/gpio driver is fine.

--- a/arch/arm/dts/mt7986a-bpi-r3-sd.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/mt7986a-bpi-r3-sd.dts
@@ -8,4 +8,5 @@
 #include "mt7986.dtsi"
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
 
 / {
@@ -39,9 +39,11 @@
 		factory {
 			label = "reset";
+			linux,code = <KEY_RESTART>;
 			gpios = <&pio 9 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		};
 
 		wps {
 			label = "wps";
+			linux,code = <KEY_WPS_BUTTON>;
 			gpios = <&pio 10 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		};
